NPC: mrs_pell
LOCATION: upper_residential_ridge
SCHEDULE: morning=home, midday=club_road, evening=home, night=home

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(mrs_pell, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: pell_plain
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MRS. PELL: "You are not calling in any official capacity, then."
  [Mrs. Pell keeps one gloved hand on the gate latch, studying Walter's coat before she studies his face.]
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  MRS. PELL: "That is almost a relief. Men with badges always arrive having already decided what sort of answer they mean to hear."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(mrs_pell, default) AND coat != plain
  TAG: pell_badge
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_short_v1
  MRS. PELL: "Officer Corwin."
  [Her expression does not change; only the gate remains half-closed.]
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v2
  MRS. PELL: "If this concerns the club, I imagine Captain Odell has already received whatever statement the town requires of me."

# Plain coat defaults: neighborly visit, gravel path, rain ruts
TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(mrs_pell, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: pell_repeat_plain_gate
  WEIGHT: 3
  [Mrs. Pell adjusts her shawl, resting her fingers upon the wrought-iron gate.]
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  MRS. PELL: "A neighborly visit is always preferable to an official summons, Walter. The ridge is quiet this hour."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(mrs_pell, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: pell_repeat_plain_wind
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: violin_cautious_short_v1
  MRS. PELL: "Mind the gravel path on the descent. The carriage ruts are deep after the rain."

# Police coat / badge defaults: closed gate, staff boundaries
TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(mrs_pell, default) AND coat != plain
  TAG: pell_repeat_badge_latched
  WEIGHT: 3
  [She keeps the iron latch firmly engaged, speaking through the bars.]
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  MRS. PELL: "The gate remains closed, Officer. The precinct has had its answers regarding the club road."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(mrs_pell, default) AND coat != plain
  TAG: pell_repeat_badge_servants
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: violin_dismissive_short_v1
  MRS. PELL: "Do not question my domestic staff without my presence, Corwin. That is all."

TOPIC: club_guests
  GATE: always
  TAG: pell_guests
  LABEL: "Ask who visited the ridge after dark"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "There were carriages on this road after midnight."
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v2
  MRS. PELL: "There are always carriages on this road after midnight. That is half the point of having a ridge to climb to."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I only need to know whose."
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v2
  MRS. PELL: "No, Officer. You need a world in which the right names make the wrong night simpler. That is not the same thing."
  NOTEBOOK: pell_ridge_traffic | "Mrs. Pell would not name late-night visitors to the ridge; she treated such traffic as routine among the upper houses."

TOPIC: servant_talk
  GATE: coat = plain
  TAG: pell_servants
  LABEL: "Ask whether her maid heard anything from the club road"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Your maid keeps the back rooms facing the club road."
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MRS. PELL: "She keeps my rooms, Officer. She is not an extension of your precinct."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did she hear anything?"
  VOICE: violin_dismissive_medium_v2
  MRS. PELL: "She heard men arriving too confident and leaving too quickly. In this town that narrows nothing."
  NOTEBOOK: pell_maid_heard | "Mrs. Pell admitted her maid heard men arriving and departing the ridge in haste, but gave no names."
  EVIDENCE: ridge_haste
  
TOPIC: crew_omission
  GATE: topic_done(local_historian, crew_omission_official) AND NOT topic_done(mrs_pell, crew_omission)
  TAG: mrs_pell_crew_omission
  LABEL: "Ask why the town's history leaves out the crew's names"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "The memorial on the common lists every owner who subscribed to the rebuilding fund.\nIt does not list the men who drowned."
  VOICE: violin_haunting_medium_v2
  MRS. PELL: "A subscription is a matter of public record.\nA drowning is a matter of the sea."
  WALTER CORWIN: "The sea didn't write the memorial. The committee did."
  [She releases the gate latch and lets it click shut between them.]
  VOICE: violin_bureaucratic_long_v1
  MRS. PELL: "My grandfather sat on that committee, Officer.\nHe was not a cruel man.\nHe was a practical one.\nThere is a difference, and it has served this ridge for a hundred years."
  WALTER CORWIN: "It served the ridge. I'm asking about the crew."
  VOICE: violin_neutral_medium_v1
  MRS. PELL: "Then ask the harbor. The harbor keeps its own account."
  NOTEBOOK: pell_crew_omission | "Mrs. Pell acknowledged her grandfather sat on the memorial committee. Framed the omission as practical rather than cruel. Referred to 'the harbor' as the keeper of a different account."